.TH CHPC-PYTHON-HELPER 1 "2026-09-29" "CHPC_python_helper 0.1.0" "Coastal HPC"
.SH NAME
chpc-python-helper \- build Python 3 scripts for airgapped RHEL/Rocky/Debian systems from a vetted template library
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B python3 -m chpc_python_helper
.I command
.RI [ arguments ... ]
.br
.B chpc-python-helper
.I command
.RI [ arguments ... ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B chpc-python-helper
builds Python 3 scripts on a machine with no network access and no AI
model involved at all -- the same tool as
.BR chpc-bash-helper ,
generating Python instead of bash. You either pick a template from its
library and answer a short series of questions, or describe what you
want in plain English and let it match your description against the
library by keyword overlap.
.PP
Every generated script is checked with
.B python3 -m py_compile
(a syntax-only compile; nothing is ever executed) before it is written
to disk. A command or value you type is safely embedded as a proper
Python literal (via
.BR repr() ),
so quotes or special characters in your input can't corrupt the
generated script's syntax.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B list
List every template in the library.
.TP
.BI show " template-id " "[--raw]"
Show what a template asks. With
.BR --raw ,
also print the template's raw, unrendered text.
.TP
.BI describe " \(dqdescription\(dq"
Rank every template by plain keyword overlap against
.IR description .
.TP
.BI build " template-id " "[options]"
Build a script from
.IR template-id .
With no
.BR --var / --toggle / --toggle-group / --yes
flags, runs an interactive wizard; with any of those, runs
non-interactively.
.SH OPTIONS FOR "BUILD"
.TP
.BI --out " path"
Where to write the generated script. Defaults to
.IR template-id .py
in the current directory.
.TP
.BI --var " NAME=VALUE"
Answer one variable non-interactively. Repeatable.
.TP
.BI --toggle " NAME=on|off"
Answer one yes/no toggle non-interactively. Repeatable.
.TP
.BI --toggle-group " NAME=VALUE"
Answer one multiple-choice group non-interactively. Repeatable.
.TP
.B --yes
Accept every default and run non-interactively.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
.RS
.EX
python3 -m chpc_python_helper list
python3 -m chpc_python_helper describe "wait for a service to be ready"
python3 -m chpc_python_helper build wait_for_condition
python3 -m chpc_python_helper build node_drain_resume \e
    --var "NODE_LIST=node042" \e
    --toggle-group "SCHEDULER=slurm" \e
    --toggle-group "ACTION=drain" \e
    --out node042_drain.py
.EE
.RE
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
An unknown template id, a malformed
.BR --var / --toggle / --toggle-group
value, a template failed its
.B py_compile
check, or the interactive wizard was cancelled.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I chpc_python_helper/library/*.json
Template metadata: title, description, tags, and declared
variables/toggles/toggle_groups.
.TP
.I chpc_python_helper/library/*.py.tmpl
The matching raw Python template text, with
.B {{VARIABLE}}
and
.B {{#TOGGLE}}...{{/TOGGLE}}
placeholders.
.TP
.I chpc_helper_core/
The shared engine (templating, wizard, matcher, CLI) this app is built
on -- must be copied alongside
.I chpc_python_helper/
as a sibling directory.
.SH SEE ALSO
The full manual,
.IR CHPC_HELPER_SUITE_MANUAL.md ,
and this package's own
.IR README.md ,
both shipped alongside this tool.
.SH AUTHOR
Coastal HPC.
